Derek,

I don't have this configuration to test.

However, RPostgreSQL uses PostgreSQL libpq so the TCP issues should be at a much lower level than R.  Are you using dbDisconnect() on the failed connection?  It does not appear that the R code calls the libpq function PQFinish for this error in the connection method.  So I would expect in R that you could/should use dbDisconnect() to clean everything up.  This might still be an error on RPostgreSQL, but will require some more investigation.

If you call dbDisconnect() on the failed connection does your TCP issue go away?

Neil

