Dear Neil,

The file to edit is configure.in and autoconf converts it to configure.
configure is called at the install time to determine the
environments for the compilation.

The tweek to use the src/libpq in darwin system is done by 
writing a variable ENABLE_LIBPQ to src/Makevars.
When the ENABLE_LIBPQ have the set content the make will use
the accompanied src/libpq. If that is an empty string, make
works just as other systems.

In the previous version of configure.in, the ENABLE_LIBPQ
was set only based on the os_type darwin.
I edited it to try to check after the trial to find the
PG_LIBDIR and still the PG_LIBDIR is empty.

The configure.in is attached along with the configure, for 
in case you don't have a working autoconf.
Note configure is compressed with bzip2, so it should be 
decompressed and replace to the latest.

> I have access to systems to test, but I don't have enough
> knowledge of how the build/runtime systems work to just go
> in and change it.  Is there any way I can help clean this up?


So, could you test with the attached configure in combination
with latest svn version?

Sincerely yours,

