Message-ID: <D447F000-F298-4B34-945F-812A16144C55@neiltiffin.com>

Tomoaki/Dirk,

I've added clientVersion string to dbGetInfo(dbDriver).  This relies on PQlibVersion(), which is only available on PostgreSQL 9.1 or later.

PQlibVersion can be marked for gcc as weakly linked and then checked at run time to make sure it's available.

Is this sufficient or do I need to do something else, in other words do I need to worry about compilers other than gcc?

Will this work on Windows?

The added code is:

    extern int PQlibVersion() __attribute__((weak));

s_object *
RS_PostgreSQL_managerInfo(Mgr_Handle * mgrHandle)
{
    . . . . . etc.
    if (PQlibVersion)
    {
        int cv, major, minor_revision, minor, revision_num;
        cv = PQlibVersion();
        major = cv / 10000;
        minor_revision = cv % 10000;
        minor = minor_revision / 100;
        revision_num = minor_revision % 100;

        char buf1[50];
        sprintf(buf1, "%d.%d.%d", major, minor, revision_num);
        SET_LST_CHR_EL(output, j++, 0, C_S_CPY(buf1));
    }
    else
    {
        /* PQlibVersion() is not available prior to PostgreSQL 9.1 */
        SET_LST_CHR_EL(output, j++, 0, C_S_CPY(""));
    }

Neil

