Hi Neil,

> Is this sufficient or do I need to do something else, in other words do I need to worry about compilers other than gcc?

CRAN policy states "Package authors should make all reasonable efforts to provide cross-platform portable code. Packages will not normally be accepted that do not run on at least two of the major R platforms."

Among the R platforms that CRAN checks, non gcc compiler is
Solaris Studio 12.3

Other known OS that will be divert from gcc are:
XCode default became llvm.
FreeBSD is going to use clang as system compiler. 

So, I think the code should be written in a way GCC independent, or at least
return some information under non-gcc environment and work fine.
Can you determine if PQlibVersion is present at compile time and 
determine the behavior?

While the server and client may use different versions because they are just communicating,
using different version of library than what was linked is not expected to work anyway.

Best regards,


